{
  "_comment": [
    "Source data for the example fixture and its golden geometry. Entirely",
    "synthetic: abstract group/route/sink names and round numbers, chosen for the",
    "structural properties the tests need rather than to resemble any real",
    "dataset.",
    "",
    "What the shape exercises:",
    "  - one source feeding six groups spanning four orders of magnitude, so the",
    "    smallest nodes are thin enough to trip the label drop rule;",
    "  - routes and sinks shared between groups, so the per-column overlap sweep",
    "    and the gap carry-over between columns both fire;",
    "  - group b reaching two different sinks through the same route, so two rows",
    "    merge into one link;",
    "  - a route used by exactly one group (passive) with a tiny flow, so a",
    "    near-zero-height node is in play.",
    "",
    "Regenerate the derived files with: node tools/generate_golden.mjs"
  ],
